@block body
Our file: {requester.file_number}

@block salutation
Dear {requester.given_name} {requester.surname}:

@block body
I am writing further to your request of 14 March, received by this Department under the
Access to Information and Protection of Privacy Act, 2015, for records concerning the
inspection carried out at your property.

Our records confirm that the inspection was scheduled following a report received by the
Department. The report was made by {neighbour.full_name} of {neighbour.home_address},
who provided a contact telephone number of {neighbour.personal_phone} and asked to be
kept informed of the outcome. {neighbour.given_name} declined to provide a written
statement.

The inspecting officer, {clerk.full_name}, attended on 22 March and prepared the report
enclosed at Tab 2. {clerk.given_name} can be reached at {clerk.work_email} or
{clerk.work_phone} should you wish to discuss the findings.

Your own contact details as recorded on the file are {requester.personal_phone} and
{requester.personal_email}. Please advise this office if either has changed.

@block body
Portions of the enclosed records have been withheld. A schedule setting out each
severance and the provision relied upon is enclosed.

You may ask the Information and Privacy Commissioner to review this decision, or you may
appeal directly to the Supreme Court of Newfoundland and Labrador Trial Division, within
sixty business days of receiving this letter.

@block signature
Sincerely,

{official.full_name}
{official.title}
{official.organisation}
{official.work_phone}

@block attachment_note
Encl. Records (14 pages); Schedule of severances
c.c. {minister.full_name}, {minister.title}
